{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5","id":1417738,"title":"How do I explain sleeping methuselah powers in V5?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-11T18:12:56-07:00","id":1417738,"title":"How do I explain sleeping methuselah powers in V5?","content":"Published material from V5 makes it quite clear that elder powers (that is, level 6+ disciplines) isn't a thing anymore, since neither Helena nor any of the extremely ancient NPCs in London has Fallen has them. I don't mind this per se - I think 6+ scores on attributes and abilities did little for the game, and it might be better off without them.<br /> <br /> But my chronicle is set in Mexico City, where Nergal/Shaitan(Huitziolopochtli lies in torpor, and has, in old canon, been affecting the city with his tremendous methuselah powers. This causes some problems. After all, there are quite a few examples in pre-V5 lore where sleeping ancients affect things in tangible ways through their powers, The Sleeping Lord in Cairo by Night being another one that I can think of.<br /> <br /> How do we explain this phenomena in V5? Could it be a case of bizarre amalgam disciplines of such high level that almost no one can unlock them (Fortitude 5 + Auspex 5 and stuff like that), or is it some other form of power unique to ancient vampires in some other way? Or should methuselah simply not have such powers anymore in V5? If so, how do we reconcile it with previous canon?<br /> <br /> open to any thoughts, as I eventually need to handle this issue in my Mexico City chronicle!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","user":"Natsymir","date":". 10-11-2020, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T18:19:56-07:00","id":1417742,"title":"","content":"I'd probably make it into some kind of Presence+Auspex amalgam, if you want to have it done mechanically, or you can just say that's because they have such thick blood [so high blood potency] they can &quot;re-roll&quot; so many times, their Disciplines work through their sleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Constantinople was <b>not</b> a mistake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26438-thedreamapologist","name":"TheDreamApologist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T18:30:25-07:00","id":1417743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Natsymir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5#post1417738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Published material from V5 makes it quite clear that elder powers (that is, level 6+ disciplines) isn't a thing anymore, since neither Helena nor any of the extremely ancient NPCs in London has Fallen has them. I don't mind this per se - I think 6+ scores on attributes and abilities did little for the game, and it might be better off without them.<br /> <br /> But my chronicle is set in Mexico City, where Nergal/Shaitan(Huitziolopochtli lies in torpor, and has, in old canon, been affecting the city with his tremendous methuselah powers. This causes some problems. After all, there are quite a few examples in pre-V5 lore where sleeping ancients affect things in tangible ways through their powers, The Sleeping Lord in Cairo by Night being another one that I can think of.<br /> <br /> How do we explain this phenomena in V5? Could it be a case of bizarre amalgam disciplines of such high level that almost no one can unlock them (Fortitude 5 + Auspex 5 and stuff like that), or is it some other form of power unique to ancient vampires in some other way? Or should methuselah simply not have such powers anymore in V5? If so, how do we reconcile it with previous canon?<br /> <br /> open to any thoughts, as I eventually need to handle this issue in my Mexico City chronicle!</div> </div> </div> </div>Combo Disciplines apparently is how this works.<br /> <br /> Just ignore the restriction against having more than one power to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T19:26:01-07:00","id":1417750,"title":"","content":"you could make Combo Disciplines,as CTPhipps said. but you could make them a little stronger,and make them only possible at a certain Blood Potency","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T17:37:05-07:00","id":1417956,"title":"","content":"Honestly, it doesn't work. It's a plot hole. The game mechanics fail to model the realities of the setting. You can bring up a bunch of other iconic methuselah feats like Michael affecting all of Constantinople with his Presence that are simply too powerful for a 5-dot amalgam, however you slice it. I don't want a vampire with Auspex 5/Presence 5/Dominate 5 able to use Presence over an entire city.<br /> <br /> There's basically three things you can do.<br /> <br /> * Have methuselah-level powers simply not exist anymore.<br /> <br /> * Declare that sufficiently ancient methuselahs, the ones just a step short of an Antediluvian's age and power (e.g., Shaitan and ur-Shulgi), can simply do things that break the rules, no game mechanics involved.<br /> <br /> * Make 6+ Disciplines a thing again.<br /> <br /> I've never cared for &quot;Devotions only possible at a certain Blood Potency,&quot; in either Masquerade or Requiem. They're 6+ Disciplines by another name. Just call a spade a spade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T17:59:55-07:00","id":1417961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1417956#post1417956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, it doesn't work. It's a plot hole. The game mechanics fail to model the realities of the setting. You can bring up a bunch of other iconic methuselah feats like Michael affecting all of Constantinople with his Presence that are simply too powerful for a 5-dot amalgam, however you slice it. I don't want a vampire with Auspex 5/Presence 5/Dominate 5 able to use Presence over an entire city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, they'd have to buy a separate power that allowed them to do it and have the Blood Potency to use it like that. So you could have, &quot;Dominate City&quot; as a Auspex 5/Presence 5/Dominate 5 as a power but have the restricture of &quot;Blood Potency 9.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which I think solves a lot of the problems right there.<br /> <br /> My answer for it in my game, which is an extension of V20 and Revised is to introduce the Withering.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>House Rule: The Withering</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Some unnatural force is sapping the strength of Elders and Methuselahs in the world. No matter how powerful they were before, any vampire who does not answer the call of the Beckoning is reduced to Level 5 Disciplines or below. They are also unable to possess Attributes or Skills over 5 points. A vampire that successfully does answer the Beckoning will be able to access their full Disciplines within the Middle East or whatever other location that they find themselves drawn to. If they are ever released from the mysterious source that pulls them, they will return with a full array of 6+ Disciplines or traits that they possessed before as well as possibly more. It is possible for Kindred to temporarily regain some of their +6 Disciplines by diablerizing other vampires with +1 point for Generations from Thin Blood to 8th generation and +1 additional point for every generation below 8th. These will last for a month until they begin fading again.</i></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T23:15:39-07:00","id":1417991,"title":"","content":"Don't combo disciplines use up the highest discipline 'slot'? So you can't have multiples, and in taking the one you can have you block yourself from the 'nornal' level power from that discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T23:30:37-07:00","id":1417992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1417991#post1417991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't combo disciplines use up the highest discipline 'slot'? So you can't have multiples, and in taking the one you can have you block yourself from the 'nornal' level power from that discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's a silly rule on top of a silly rule.<br /> <br /> I love V5 but while I understand the desire to game balance, if you can afford the Discipline powers then you should be able to buy as many Combos and Powers as you want.<br /> <br /> What I want most from THE PLAYERS GUIDE is:<br /> <br /> * Elder Powers<br /> * Optional rules for multiple powers of the same levels<br /> * Clan Tzimisce<br /> * Remnant Sabbat (I don't expect to get this)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T02:17:20-07:00","id":1418002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1417956#post1417956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, it doesn't work. It's a plot hole. The game mechanics fail to model the realities of the setting. You can bring up a bunch of other iconic methuselah feats like Michael affecting all of Constantinople with his Presence that are simply too powerful for a 5-dot amalgam, however you slice it. I don't want a vampire with Auspex 5/Presence 5/Dominate 5 able to use Presence over an entire city.<br /> <br /> There's basically three things you can do.<br /> <br /> * Have methuselah-level powers simply not exist anymore.<br /> <br /> * Declare that sufficiently ancient methuselahs, the ones just a step short of an Antediluvian's age and power (e.g., Shaitan and ur-Shulgi), can simply do things that break the rules, no game mechanics involved.<br /> <br /> * Make 6+ Disciplines a thing again.<br /> <br /> I've never cared for &amp;quot;Devotions only possible at a certain Blood Potency,&amp;quot; in either Masquerade or Requiem. They're 6+ Disciplines by another name. Just call a spade a spade.</div> </div> </div> </div>And who decides that high powered amalgams can\u2019t be as powerful or more powerful than the old 6+ disciplines?<br /> <br /> No one but the ST. You can in fact have amalgams duplicate all the old \u201celder powers\u201d or you can have lvl 5 disciplines do so (although I don\u2019t think you should). <br /> <br /> It\u2019s just a matter of understanding that mechanics may have changed but all that was possible before still is right now. <br /> <br /> As others have said there\u2019s a limit that needs to be removed abd that\u2019s the amount of discipline powers one vampire can have (which I agree was a silly rule geared towards neonates but it is easily remedied I myself posted house rules to make elders as powerful as the story needs them to be).<br /> <br /> Aside from that only tangible difference between V5 and older editions is the fact that THEORETICALLY a 13th gen vampire can access elder powers as they are not gated by generation anymore. Is that a bad thing? I\u2019m not dure it is, \u00e8 special lu considering how the old elder powers were mostly meant as ST tools for their NPCs, and were honestly an inchoerent mess with some lower generation powers being weaker/less useful than the higher gen ones","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T12:11:39-07:00","id":1418078,"title":"","content":"Its unexplainable with V5 RAW. You have to merely resort to house-rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T17:11:00-07:00","id":1418121,"title":"","content":"There's a Dominate Amalgam listed on the White Wolf Wiki that is a V5 version of the old level 9 Dominate power. Not to mention some of the old 6+ level powers got worked in to the main V5 book Disciplines. So all you need is a good house rule for older vampires not being capped at five powers per Discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T17:22:09-07:00","id":1418123,"title":"","content":"Alas some players have this attitude regarding House Rules.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://ryanainsworthimedia.files.wordpress.com/2014/01/original.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T23:29:21-07:00","id":1418152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1418002#post1418002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And who decides that high powered amalgams can\u2019t be as powerful or more powerful than the old 6+ disciplines?<br /> <br /> No one but the ST. You can in fact have amalgams duplicate all the old \u201celder powers\u201d or you can have lvl 5 disciplines do so (although I don\u2019t think you should).</div> </div> </div> </div>The ST can also say that level 4, level 3, or even level 1 amalgams are as powerful as 6+ Disciplines. Their game. That doesn't mean it's good mechanics design, as I consider it to remove the meaning behind the numbers. Michael's A Perfect World power is a whole 'nother league beyond what Presence 5 can do. So I don't want A Perfect World to be Presence 5. It is a superior power, ergo it should have a higher number.<br /> <br /> Many of the published 6+ Disciplines were underpowered and shouldn't have been 6+ Disciplines. But there are plenty of godly methuselah feats, like Menele destroying Pompeii, or that Dominate power to compel all of your descendants everywhere across the world, which are way beyond what level 5 powers can do. So where does that leave designers?<br /> <br /> 1. &quot;Make A Perfect World an Auspex 5/Dominate 5/Presence 5 amalgam.&quot; -&gt; Problematic because a 13th-generation neonate could have that amalgam. Yes, GMs can just decide not to let 13th-generation neonates have those amalgams. That doesn't solve my problem. I don't want it to be theoretically possible under the rules and denied by GM fiat. I want it to be impossible under the rules, because I want the rules to model the realities of the setting.<br /> <br /> 2. &quot;Make A Perfect World a Presence 5 amalgam with a Blood Potency 9 requirement.&quot; -&gt; Just call a spade a spade. This makes it an elder Discipline in everything but name. Also, problematic because you could have a Gangrel methuselah with Presence 5 and Blood Potency 9 who could learn A Perfect World. I don't want that Gangrel methuselah with a &quot;dip investment&quot; in Presence able to perform the same Presence feats as Michael. I only want a vampire with Presence 9 able to perform the same Presence feats as Michael.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well just don't let the Gangrel methuselah have A Perfect World, problem solved.&quot; -&gt; See answer to #1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Aside from that only tangible difference between V5 and older editions is the fact that THEORETICALLY a 13th gen vampire can access elder powers as they are not gated by generation anymore. Is that a bad thing? I\u2019m not dure it is, \u00e8 special lu considering how the old elder powers were mostly meant as ST tools for their NPCs, and were honestly an inchoerent mess with some lower generation powers being weaker/less useful than the higher gen ones </div> </div> </div>I think it is. I don't want 13th-generation vampires able to enslave or destroy entire cities.<br /> <br /> 100% agreed though, many of the elder Disciplines we got were either badly designed or work better as 1-5 powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":3110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","user":"False Epiphany","date":". 10-23-2020, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T00:54:50-07:00","id":1418155,"title":"","content":"I disagree with that notion that the Elder disciplines were badly designed. They were extremely good, potent, and very fun to use if you had the gumption to actually get to that point or started your chronicle in earlier ages and worked up to the Final Nights era (of which your PCs would either be Elders or Methuselahs themselves depending on the specific time you started the chronicle). I still don't know why people even think these powers were only meant to be ST NPC powers... where do people get this idea? Tabletop isn't like video games where certain things are locked out for the sake of video-game balance or just being part of the story fiat... Tabletop is one of the most flexible game mediums with an open world as far as your imagination... Why is it of the belief that PCs can't obtain these powers whatsoever if they are the sufficient generation (whether through diablerie or simply being embraced to said theoretical generation) and built up the skill to get to that obtaination?<br /> <br /> It completely breaks the setting nowadays where people evoke that 13 gens can now do Elder and Methuselah tier powers, complete sun-rocket dodo-flying nonsense. I truly wonder why this route was taken to do such deleterious nerfs and whatever this Amalgam system is. People continue to criticize oWoD mechanics.. but fail to realize the entire thing was near-perfect, with it only needing a few touch-ups here and there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 10-14-2020, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T09:10:46-07:00","id":1418201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1418155#post1418155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It completely breaks the setting nowadays where people evoke that 13 gens can now do Elder and Methuselah tier powers, complete sun-rocket dodo-flying nonsense. I truly wonder why this route was taken to do such deleterious nerfs and whatever this Amalgam system is. People continue to criticize oWoD mechanics.. but fail to realize the entire thing was near-perfect, with it only needing a few touch-ups here and there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they can. I think people have basically just ignored Blood Potency as a thing from centuries of experience as a way to make it so that its HARDER for Neonates not to be able to God Tier stuff if they have the right generation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T11:14:20-07:00","id":1418220,"title":"","content":"There's no legal way to do it, beyond the golden rule (if that's still a thing)<br /> <br /> Maybe you could have all the characters in the city just <i>imagine </i>there's a sleeping methuselah watching them. Maybe they're all crazy. maybe there's something in the air. Since you're using Baali, maybe it's a big awesome demon. There aren't rules for demons yet.<br /> <br /> (also 6+ ability scores were great because you can mostly do what you want with them, and getting down to 7th or even 6th generation so you can transcend earthly limitations was an achievable and desirable goal for players. You want ambitious players at your table. They're the interesting ones. The V5 system doesn't encourage that)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T12:35:21-07:00","id":1418230,"title":"","content":"But yes, the biggest hole in the game now is omnipotent god powers for methuselahs.<br /> <br /> Which are an ingrained part of the setting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T14:34:46-07:00","id":1418247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Natsymir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5#post1417738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do I explain sleeping methuselah powers in V5?</div> </div> </div> </div>blood sorcery ritual,<br /> <br /> from what I heard, there's a blood sorcery ritual in London that allows an elder to feed by proxy<br /> <br /> there's also the Tokyo thing where the local vampires don't feel hunger, which is probably an elder pulling some blood sorcery ritual out of their ass<br /> <br /> and...well it's just the classic VtM special. whenever you don't know how to explain something...BLOOD MAGIC<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T18:01:53-07:00","id":1418276,"title":"","content":"How can a Torpored Vampire do a ritual when it's asleep? Rituals as part of the namesake need to be actively worked on and managed. A sleeping Methuselah or Antediluvian do their abilities unconsciously with simply the power of their Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T04:13:03-07:00","id":1418335,"title":"","content":"Shaitan is an infernal lord,<br /> let his cultists maintain the ritual","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T06:19:12-07:00","id":1418351,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't do it trough Blood Sorcery, because that's a single Discipline to have at 5.<br /> <br /> It solves none of the perceived problems of &quot;uber amalgams&quot;, and brings it's own problems. And now Tremere are the one and only clan that has the cheapest way to &quot;elder powers&quot; - I don't think that was ever the intention.<br /> <br /> If these rituals can't be just learned/invented by anyone with BM 5, then it's just a macguffin. Not much different from just saying &quot;elders have narrative powers outside the scope of the game&quot;<br /> <br /> I think uber-amalgams are still the best answer (that's not, &quot;use V20 &gt; rules&quot;).<br /> <br /> They're too expensive for a realistic Neonate to ever buy (before &quot;graduating&quot; to a less aggravating nickname, that is). Also we don't know how these are created: one could get clever here and put requisites that a &quot;Neonate&quot; would find hard (but, I say, not impossible) to fulfill. And they can allways include Blood Magic as a necessary requisite (one can always pour moar magic into the soup, and trully great Elders always seem to have ritual powers for some reason)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-15-2020, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T07:58:29-07:00","id":1418366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1418351#post1418351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't do it trough Blood Sorcery, because that's a single Discipline to have at 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking multiple cultists with thaum 5 or whatevs,<br /> they draw the potent blood from their Lord (as their own blood wouldn't be potent enough),<br /> and then use it for the ritual, takes however long it takes,<br /> they drink or paint some of the blood in Aztec rituals with neo pagan mortals/sorcerers,<br /> and Nergal's will is done<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think uber-amalgams are still the best answer (that's not, &quot;use V20 &gt; rules&quot;). </div> </div> </div>I don't mind the uber-amalgams (v20 rules suck, so do amalgams)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're too expensive for a realistic Neonate to ever buy (before &quot;graduating&quot; to a less aggravating nickname, that is). </div> </div> </div>that's actually a flaw, I don't see why I need to be 600 years old before I can do cool stuff<br /> <br /> I'm excited for when they publish M5, where mages have to pay for rotes and all paradigms are unified like the v5 humanity system","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T10:29:08-07:00","id":1418392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1418366#post1418366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that's actually a flaw, I don't see why I need to be 600 years old before I can do cool stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, someone could say that if everyone can do it, it's no longer special (and if people have problems understanding how the SI it's such a treath NOW, imagine with 10 years old leeches being able to control whole cities).<br /> <br /> But to each it's own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm excited for when they publish M5, where mages have to<b><i> pay for rotes</i> </b>and <b><i>all paradigms are unified</i></b> like the v5 humanity system </div> </div> </div>I HOPE you're being sarcastic...<br /> <br /> (well, if rotes *do* something more than a -1 to the diff, I won't mind paying for them)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-15-2020, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T12:01:51-07:00","id":1418400,"title":"","content":"Just assume the elders have unique powers, and that's it. Kind of like special loresheets for them. No need of special disciplines. Each elder can have different powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25881-mr-stick","name":"Mr. Stick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T13:54:49-07:00","id":1418408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1418392#post1418392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, someone could say that if everyone can do it, it's no longer special (and if people have problems understanding how the SI it's such a treath NOW, imagine with 10 years old leeches being able to control whole cities).<br /> <br /> But to each it's own.</div> </div> </div> </div>most elder powers, combo disciplines and amalgams aren't that special, <br /> it takes less than a 100 years for mages and sorcerers to achieve the same if not better,<br /> and humans can already use consensual technomancy for free<br /> <br /> I don't know why my vampire should wait a millenia to achieve the same,<br /> and even then I'm not asking for god powers, I just want to do cool stuff like teleport or walk on walls without having to pay for gated and overpriced 6+ disciplines or amalgams,<br /> <br /> hell, why do I even need a discipline to get night vision, heightened senses or claws? I'm a freaking vampire, I should have those for free<br /> <br /> the last two VtM video games had<br /> - a year old lasombra that had potence, could teleport through shadows, call onto spectres to affect the material world and manipulate memories,<br /> - a neonate that could stand up to true mages,<br /> <br /> and those were great<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I HOPE you're being sarcastic...<br /> <br /> (well, if rotes *do* something more than a -1 to the diff, I won't mind paying for them) </div> </div> </div>if Mage gets the same treatment as VtM, it's definitely what's gonna happen<br /> <br /> to do fireballs, Tremere have to prepare a ritual for 5 or 10 minutes before they can use it...once<br /> <br /> imagine your Mercurial having to spend 10 minutes to cast an Arc rote<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T14:15:00-07:00","id":1418411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1418230#post1418230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yes, the biggest hole in the game now is omnipotent god powers for methuselahs.<br /> <br /> Which are an ingrained part of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Isn't intrinsically part of the setting jump to v5 that any elder who stayed around LOST their godlike power in exchange for ignoring the beckoning? Isn't that even the impetus of the Fall of London Adventure that Mithras is a shell of his godlike self and wants that power back? Vampire has its Avatar Storm equivalent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T14:19:25-07:00","id":1418415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1418411#post1418411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't intrinsically part of the setting jump to v5 that any elder who stayed around LOST their godlike power in exchange for ignoring the beckoning? Isn't that even the impetus of the Fall of London Adventure that Mithras is a shell of his godlike self and wants that power back? Vampire has its Avatar Storm equivalent.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. No, literally, I made that up as a house rule and gave an explanation for such in this thread.<br /> <br /> 2. Mithras is a shell of his former self because he's in Monty Coven's body and doesn't have all of his memories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T22:12:30-07:00","id":1418482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Stick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1418400#post1418400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just assume the elders have unique powers, and that's it. Kind of like special loresheets for them. No need of special disciplines. Each elder can have different powers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See this attitude doesn't take into account the reality of tabletop. What if the PCs are Elders themselves? Where are the mechanics to adequately represent and phase this in gameplay whatsoever? This shafting and capping of Disciplines goes on the assumption that everyone needs to tow the same style of RP (that is the assumption that people want to blindly only play Neonates for the whole of the chronicle and never developing their characters further with adequate narrative time-skips) and isn't modular like how V20 was. 6+ Disciplines weren't &quot;special&quot; disciplines nor does it make a splick of sense for EVERY ELDER TO HAVE DIFFERENT POWERS within the same Disciplines nonsensically.<br /> <br /> Discplines are tied to the bloodline you came from or if outside of your clan niche, learned from an associate who knows the Discipline your seeking- there is no out of the blue &quot;different powers&quot; from nowhere unless you pioneer it with significant long investment or mutate into an entirely new bloodline somehow (the latter being the most common case; of which this is the only point the talk of &quot;special disciplines&quot; is remotely true.. and they were never the norm). There were supposed to be signals of the growing proficiency you garner in a Discipline as you roll with the ages. High level 6+ Disciplines found in the older editions weren't &quot;special&quot; in the sense of how you put it, but special in the fact you survived and overcame long enough to get to that point and from a meta prospective you should be rewarded for that.<br /> <br /> They are &quot;unique&quot; only for the sense of Neonates and Anchillae who don't possess them because they feel so far out of reach, but the ones who were smart and adaptable, the ones who don't meet Final Death to grow more powerful know all to well of the growing benefits of age (barring out the negative side-effects that follow too). Among peers however, this growth isn't unique and plays intrinsically of how the setting functions in the terms of escalating supernatural powers against one another, i.e the Jyhad. The tenuous proxy plays, schemes, the power a childe covets toward their sires, maneuvering, all amplified by the power of the Disciplines are what made VTM. All this could also be experienced by the players further down the line, but it has been shirked for whatever this &quot;reworked&quot; system is that can't mechanically and meta-wise demonstrate feats we see from the lore within the game; nor players themselves as I touched earlier can participate in the higher tiers of the VTM Jyhad. Maybe I'm wrong and we will see the return of 6+ powers in newer supplements and the capping could be temporary as the finer details of V5 get worked out, but my hopes are genuinely not high at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T05:39:45-07:00","id":1418505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are &quot;unique&quot; only for the sense of Neonates and Anchillae who don't possess them because they feel so far out of reach, but the ones who were smart and adaptable, the ones who don't meet Final Death to grow more powerful know all to well of the growing benefits of age</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that and the benefit of eating your Elders. Unless you were very low generation yourself, which from a players perspective was unlikely<br /> <br /> V5 does a better service to the power of <i>age</i><i> and experience</i> - because the former gives you Blood Potency, and the latter it's the only thing gating max level powers (regardless of the fact that such maximum it's not that impressive rigth now, albeit it could be with some tweaking). Before age was merely xp, which could traduce to loads of Disciplines at 5, and even the old version of amalgams, but no actual Elder power","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T07:46:17-07:00","id":1418526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1418505#post1418505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> V5 does a better service to the power of <i>age</i><i> and experience</i> - because the former gives you Blood Potency, and the latter it's the only thing gating max level powers (regardless of the fact that such maximum it's not that impressive rigth now, albeit it could be with some tweaking). Before age was merely xp, which could traduce to loads of Disciplines at 5, and even the old version of amalgams, but no actual Elder power</div> </div> </div> </div>whut? No. <br /> <br /> Blood potency is shit. I don't want to eat my way up to godhood when doing so limits who i feed from, increases my base hunger, and 'godhood' only means a few extra dice for the shitty 1-5 discipline range everyone else is confined to. <br /> <br /> The power of Generation was simple: More blood, faster blood, and a higher ceiling for power. Oh and some minor stuff like Dominate and better ghouls. You weren't supposed to juice up through Diablerie. Diablerie wasn't &quot;The quick and dirty path to power&quot;, It wasn't the Dark side of the Force, you weren't meant to gamble away your humanity for a game-breaking fuckton of XP. Diablerie was <i>the only path to new heights of power. </i>Everyone learns things at the same rate, lower generations can keep learning past the point the higher gens have to stop at. Very old, high gen vampires having lots of disciplines, attributes and abilities at 5 was <i>the point</i>. They <i>needed </i>to diablerize if they were to get better. And having more disciplines at 5 was a lot more useful than less disciplines at 5 and some extra blood potency dice. A <i>need </i>to do horrible things like Diablerie while not falling to the Beast is why vampires make such a big deal out of <i>the Jyhad/the struggle </i>and <i>A Beast I am lest a Beast I become. </i> V5 makes Diablerie a shitty shortcut to power you don't want with more side effects than you want and seems pretty moralizing out of it. You become a Beast if you diablerize and the 'benefit' preventing you from becoming a beast is marginal if it exists at all. So more a <i>A Beast I am to become a Beast. </i> Hardly an engaging moral quandary. Growing old in V5 is just screwing yourself as you become hungrier, pickier and there's still no way to get cooler powers beyond storyteller fiat. Growing old in prior editions got you all the XP you needed and you could go High with it if low gen and wide with it if high gen. It was mechanically, logistically, and thematically a better system. The old system matched the Fluff it came with. The new system does not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T19:21:14-07:00","id":1418625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1418123#post1418123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alas some players have this attitude regarding House Rules.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://ryanainsworthimedia.files.wordpress.com/2014/01/original.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>This is me, all the way!<br /> <br /> I think that V5 is still very new and they haven't released as many books to cover all there is in their previous editions. Even V20 seems thin compared to everything there was in revised era, though it was supposed to be so as it is, a nostalgia compilation of previous material.<br /> <br /> I personally dislike V5 and will keep playing Revised or V20 unless they release proper elder ruling and or until they do cover the basics of VtM (all clans and all sects). But when it comes to methuselah level powers, they might release it in the upcoming books, so just wait a bit longer or continue with previous edition rules.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T10:09:57-07:00","id":1418849,"title":"","content":"There's always the possibility that the game is lying to everyone, and that those things still do exist. Just imagine. Neonates, who are childer of barely Neonates themselves, are being told what the rules are. Maybe Level 6 Discipline powers still do exist, but the new characters aren't going to be told that. I'm thinking that Elder always had to ability to create new low level (1-5) powers as well as higher ones, but usually made sure that the standard powers were taught. With the Beckoning, the lock on the other low level powers was broken, and the variants became known once again. Something similar could be happening with the physical Disciplines as well. With no Elders saying otherwise, Neonates are learning of new ways of working with them. This could also be a way of explaining away the lack of Disciplines. Most Neonates don't know of the differences, so they are accidentally combining them, even when they aren't exactly the same. Newbies don't realize just how different things really are, and they are being lied to. No one know about the Banu Haqim, so of course they don't have a separate Quietus Discipline. The Banu Haqim knows, but they won't tell anyone. Something similar is going on with Thaumaturgy. The Tremere won't tell anyone, even their youngest Childer, the full truths about how the Discipline is breaking. This is an explanation for why there aren't any Paths. The are still out there, somewhere, but new characters no longer have the access to them. This is a good way to bring everything back if the IP returns to someone else, and the public opinion leans more towards the older edition rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T08:15:35-07:00","id":1419006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1417992#post1417992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that's a silly rule on top of a silly rule.<br /> <br /> I love V5 but while I understand the desire to game balance, if you can afford the Discipline powers then you should be able to buy as many Combos and Powers as you want.<br /> <br /> What I want most from THE PLAYERS GUIDE is:<br /> <br /> * Elder Powers<br /> * Optional rules for multiple powers of the same levels<br /> * Clan Tzimisce<br /> * Remnant Sabbat (I don't expect to get this)</div> </div> </div> </div>I've heard that this is happening (V5 Player's Guide), but nothing as to when it will actually be released.<br /> <br /> I do think that what you outline would be great material in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">R<i>emember, remember, the Fifth of November, the Gunpowder Treason and Plot. I know of no reason why the Gunpowder Treason should ever be forgot.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> -V for Vendetta</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","name":"Japheth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar997_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T09:10:22-07:00","id":1419016,"title":"","content":"I think they thought buying the same powers from the same level would convolute an already convoluted system.<br /> Also, yeah, they want vampires to have 'unique' powers from the get go (even though that's dumb and in a lot of powers there are easy-good choices and easy-trap choices) so letting players buy the powers they missed would de-uniquify vampire powers (Not having unique powers till 6 was the intention of four editions of vampire... combo disciplines were more perks and boosts than unique tricks...)<br /> <br /> Elder powers don't belong in a player's guide.<br /> Well, maybe 6 and 7 do because they inspire a player to ambition... but then again ambition is badwrongfun and v5 is about being persecuted for <i>sucking</i>.<br /> <br /> Also if they get 6+ powers I'll want my darn Thaumaturgy paths back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T09:21:20-07:00","id":1419019,"title":"","content":"So I'm a storyteller and I'm finishing my second V5 chronicle.<br /> Unfortunately V5 does not reach the expectations of me and most of the players in my group.<br /> The rules are simple and great, Hunger dices, tests and rolls are quick and interesting, but I'm tired of waiting for the other clans, sects, corrections for high-level disciplines and elders.<br /> <br /> For me the V5 is an incomplete product, unfortunately lost between being closer to the expectations of its hardcore fans and the politically correct.<br /> The delay in delivering the secrets related to clans, sects, powerful personalities and appropriate rules for elders and matus\u00e1lens and boring and anti climax.<br /> <br /> It is hard to believe mechanically by the rules that Theo Bell could kill Hardstadt and Peterzoon just by firing his shotgun with dragonbreath rounds (as if Fortitude just doesn't exist or if no Archon or Elder didn't react to Theo Bell's actions, even if Bell had an entire coterie de Brujahs by your side it is impossible to believe that these events took place in a Conclave in this way, we have to force our imagination to imagine Theo Bell obtaining several critical successes and imagine 20 or 30 vampires watching it without reaction and Fortitude failing !!! twice since Jan Peterzoon had the same fate ...<br /> <br /> Another lazy decision for me is to transform Protean / Serpentis, Thaumaturgy / Quietus and Obtenebration / Necr\u00f4mancia, the adaptations that are made by the fans are much better than the original material, unfortunately.<br /> <br /> Honestly, please write again Vampire and reconsider all easy rule choices and do something better and closer to the original Vampire.<br /> <br /> Keep the rules of dice rolling simple, great concepts like Hunger dice, but give support to all clans, sects, rules for elders and matusalens, and please reconsider these absurd stories like Theo Bell killing Elders without any basis for the rules.<br /> <br /> I still have to acknowledge that Chicago by Night and Fall the London are great supplements, but Helena and Mithras are just shadows compared to their previous terrifying versions.<br /> <br /> I'm going back to the V20 ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T09:55:44-07:00","id":1419027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me the V5 is an incomplete product, unfortunately lost between being closer to the expectations of its hardcore fans <b>and the politically correct.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>This sets off all manner of red flags.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1419019#post1419019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is hard to believe mechanically by the rules that Theo Bell could kill Hardstadt and Peterzoon just by firing his shotgun with dragonbreath rounds (as if Fortitude just doesn't exist or if no Archon or Elder didn't react to Theo Bell's actions, even if Bell had an entire coterie de Brujahs by your side it is impossible to believe that these events took place in a Conclave in this way, we have to force our imagination to imagine Theo Bell obtaining several critical successes and imagine 20 or 30 vampires watching it without reaction and Fortitude failing !!! twice since Jan Peterzoon had the same fate ...</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like you miss the point of that scene given Theo Bell was executing a suicide attack. The fact that the Brujah helped him escape is why they were exiled from the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> And it sounds silly that, &quot;A point blank shotgun to the chin of Hardelstadt the Younger didn't kill him but he finished him off the next round.&quot; Even if he did, they're not going to describe it that way. The reason that it DID succeed, though, is because that Hardelstadt the Younger is almost certainly Jurgen rather than a Methusaleh. He's much younger and weaker than the vampire he's pretending to be.<br /> <br /> The Brujah were correct to help Bell in his assassination attempt and this is not even the first time this has happened as they protected Tyler when she tried to kill Hardelstadt at the Convention of Thorns.<br /> <br /> Theo Bell also states outright he did NOT kill Jan Pieterszoon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, please write again Vampire and reconsider all easy rule choices and do something better and closer to the original Vampire. </div> </div> </div>I hope they don't. I have my own issues but I just wish we'd get the final clans and rules updates instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-19-2020, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T09:59:22-07:00","id":1419030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Japheth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1419006#post1419006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've heard that this is happening (V5 Player's Guide), but nothing as to when it will actually be released.<br /> <br /> I do think that what you outline would be great material in it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Basically the only thing from CTPhipps' wish list that was on the docket for the PG was Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> We've been flatly told there are no plans for Elder-specific powers, the Tzimisce writeup was already kicked back once for being 'too Sabbat' (basically WW has kicked anything that had a 'here is what the Sabbat is now' focus, likely because they are still building that), so there's no plans for Sabbat-related stuff in it.<br /> <br /> The only up in the air might be 'more than one power per level for elders,' but probably not, as everything else written and said by various involved people has mentioned that limitation is also in place by WW so far, just like no elder stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T13:08:33-07:00","id":1419207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1419027#post1419027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This sets off all manner of red flags.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I feel like you miss the point of that scene given Theo Bell was executing a suicide attack. The fact that the Brujah helped him escape is why they were exiled from the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> And it sounds silly that, &quot;A point blank shotgun to the chin of Hardelstadt the Younger didn't kill him but he finished him off the next round.&quot; Even if he did, they're not going to describe it that way. The reason that it DID succeed, though, is because that Hardelstadt the Younger is almost certainly Jurgen rather than a Methusaleh. He's much younger and weaker than the vampire he's pretending to be.<br /> <br /> The Brujah were correct to help Bell in his assassination attempt and this is not even the first time this has happened as they protected Tyler when she tried to kill Hardelstadt at the Convention of Thorns.<br /> <br /> Theo Bell also states outright he did NOT kill Jan Pieterszoon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I hope they don't. I have my own issues but I just wish we'd get the final clans and rules updates instead.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In Giovanni Chronicles Hardestadt the Younger is really powerful elder (Auxpes 2, Celerty 5, Dominate 7, Fortitude 5, Necromancy 1, Potence 6, Presence 5, Protean 4), Bell never can make one (ou more) easly kill shot against Hardestadt, in Convention of Thorns is a mess, many clans and personalities and not all is loyal to new sect, Tyler shot and your weapon cause no harm to Hardestad and all witnes maybe see this action of Tyler, patetic.<br /> <br /> In Prague Conclave i imagine archons, hounds, elders and justicar reunited, loyal and ready to duty, i cant imagine 5 clans, and armed ghouls and other vampires make nothing against Bell and others Brujahs. <br /> <br /> My inglish sucks, sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T13:20:54-07:00","id":1419212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1419207#post1419207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In Giovanni Chronicles Hardestadt the Younger is really powerful elder (Auxpes 2, Celerty 5, Dominate 7, Fortitude 5, Necromancy 1, Potence 6, Presence 5, Protean 4), Bell never can make one (ou more) easly kill shot against Hardestadt, in Convention of Thorns is a mess, many clans and personalities and not all is loyal to new sect, Tyler shot and your weapon cause no harm to Hardestad and all witnes maybe see this action of Tyler, patetic.<br /> <br /> In Prague Conclave i imagine archons, hounds, elders and justicar reunited, loyal and ready to duty, i cant imagine 5 clans, and armed ghouls and other vampires make nothing against Bell and others Brujahs.<br /> <br /> My inglish sucks, sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Notably, the stats given for Hardelstadt the &quot;Younger&quot; list his generation wrong so that would be the stats for Hardelstadt the Elder. Mind you, the whole plotline with him is because of an editorial mistake.<br /> <br /> And you misremember because in the Convention of Thorns, ALL OF THE BRUJAH and former Anarchs protect Tyler's escape.<br /> <br /> Her actions inspire half of them to reject the peace offering and to form the Sabbat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T17:31:21-07:00","id":1419269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1419207#post1419207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In Giovanni Chronicles Hardestadt the Younger is really powerful elder (Auxpes 2, Celerty 5, Dominate 7, Fortitude 5, Necromancy 1, Potence 6, Presence 5, Protean 4), Bell never can make one (ou more) easly kill shot against Hardestadt, in Convention of Thorns is a mess, many clans and personalities and not all is loyal to new sect, Tyler shot and your weapon cause no harm to Hardestad and all witnes maybe see this action of Tyler, patetic.<br /> <br /> In Prague Conclave i imagine archons, hounds, elders and justicar reunited, loyal and ready to duty, i cant imagine 5 clans, and armed ghouls and other vampires make nothing against Bell and others Brujahs.<br /> <br /> My inglish sucks, sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>During the Convention of Thorns, Hardestadt's stats are more towards his' in GCI (1444 and Haceldema happening in 1493; Auspex 2, Celerity 4, Dominate 5, Fortitude 4, Potence 4, Presence 5, Protean 2) than his stats in GCII (stated above) which happened in 1666.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T18:03:28-07:00","id":1419274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1419269#post1419269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> During the Convention of Thorns, Hardestadt's stats are more towards his' in GCI (1444 and Haceldema happening in 1493; Auspex 2, Celerity 4, Dominate 5, Fortitude 4, Potence 4, Presence 5, Protean 2) than his stats in GCII (stated above) which happened in 1666.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, were I STing the Convention of Prague, I would say, &quot;Hardelstadt is terribly wounded and entering torpor. What do you do?&quot;<br /> <br /> All Kindred around him: A shame if something happened to him.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T09:25:31-07:00","id":1419384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1419269#post1419269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> During the Convention of Thorns, Hardestadt's stats are more towards his' in GCI (1444 and Haceldema happening in 1493; Auspex 2, Celerity 4, Dominate 5, Fortitude 4, Potence 4, Presence 5, Protean 2) than his stats in GCII (stated above) which happened in 1666.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's almost like there is some level of mystery intentionally left in it, for STs to play with and use as they want, and to provide drama and mystery to the setting. Perhaps it's an inside job (clearly intimated in the Cam book), perhaps Hardestadt was slain not by Bell directly (because the core book says he fired the shots that started the melee) but by others. Perhaps he faked his own death with a body double! <br /> <br /> Not every event needs to have all the minutiae explained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T13:37:25-07:00","id":1419423,"title":"","content":"Sometimes you botch even when you have a lot of dice. Apparently, that happened with Hardy's soak roll. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T16:53:44-07:00","id":1419482,"title":"","content":"Honestly? The greater part of the &quot;elder powers&quot; were just fat, only justifiable as 6+ powers due to the restrictive straightjacket manner in which vampiric powers were enforced through disciplines, in comparison with the much greater freedom and versatility one could get with Garou gifts, Awakened rotes, not to mention rituals and magic objects for both.<br /> <br /> Someone here remembers the time when you had to <i>pay a merit</i> to have your eyes shine a different color or turn into an alternative animal form with Protean?!).<br /> <br /> Oh, V5 eliminated elder powers? Whatever 2/3 of them were wastes of space anyway. Turned most of them into amalgams/combos/devotions/whatever-you-call-those the moment VtDA reintroduced the concept into the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> Quick, dirty &amp; simple examples:<br /> - Disguising one's aura? Auspex 2, Obfuscate 4.<br /> - Disguising one's thoughts? Auspex 4, Obfuscate 4.<br /> - Having some self-awareness while in torpor? Auspex 5, Fortitude 3+ (it let's you tank <i>aggravated damage</i>, letting you endure sleep seems valid).<br /> - Animalism 4 or Dominate 5, Fortitude 3+ for occasionally leaving one's sleeping carcass to glimpse the world - or act upon it - through other's eyes.<br /> - Dominating a bunch of people in sight? &quot;All Eyes On Me&quot; Dominate 3+, Presence 5.<br /> <br /> So on and so long....If an &quot;elder power&quot; is just a &quot;quickfix&quot;, slight upgrade or countermove to a lvl 1-5 power, just rewrite it into a combo, merit (animal succulence) or whatever.<br /> Does any of those examples help with Shaitan doing sleeping methuselah shenanigans, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir\">Natsymir</a>?<br /> <br /> Elder powers i reserve for <b>really </b>hardcore &quot;Pompeii &amp; Herculanum burn again at level 7-8&quot; stuff. That simple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-21-2020, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T19:35:40-07:00","id":1419501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1419482#post1419482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disguising one's aura? Auspex 2, Obfuscate 4</div> </div> </div> </div>And then eliminate your chance to buy the power to trick surveilance cameras. Forever.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Disguising one's thoughts? Auspex 4, Obfuscate 4. </div> </div> </div>And then eliminate your chance to buy the power that let you read auras. Forever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Having some self-awareness while in torpor? Auspex 5, Fortitude 3+ (it let's you tank aggravated damage, letting you endure sleep seems valid). </div> </div> </div>And then eliminate your chance to buy the power that let you read minds. Forever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Animalism 4 or Dominate 5, Fortitude 3+ for occasionally leaving one's sleeping carcass to glimpse the world - or act upon it - through other's eyes. </div> </div> </div>And then eliminate your chance to buy the power that let you dominate crowds, and Terminal Decree. Forever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So on and so long....If an &quot;elder power&quot; is just a &quot;quickfix&quot;, slight upgrade or countermove to a lvl 1-5 power, just rewrite it into a combo, merit (animal succulence) or whatever. </div> </div> </div>ONLY if you are the ST. If you are the player and IDK, want your elder PC buy the elder power that let you cause earthquakes (Animalism 6, &quot;Song in the Dark&quot;) your st can easily say no. And as there is nothing in the v5 rules to support you, you will have no argument to contest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T20:54:22-07:00","id":1419504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1419501#post1419501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And then eliminate your chance to buy the power to trick surveilance cameras. Forever.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And then eliminate your chance to buy the power that let you read auras. Forever.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And then eliminate your chance to buy the power that let you read minds. Forever.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And then eliminate your chance to buy the power that let you dominate crowds, and Terminal Decree. Forever.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ONLY if you are the ST. If you are the player and IDK, want your elder PC buy the elder power that let you cause earthquakes (Animalism 6, &quot;Song in the Dark&quot;) your st can easily say no. And as there is nothing in the v5 rules to support you, you will have no argument to contest.</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly do you think is the lost power?<br /> <br /> Frankly, STs should have some flexibility about what power you lose with a combo discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T23:57:14-07:00","id":1419524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1419274#post1419274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind you, were I STing the Convention of Prague, I would say, &quot;Hardelstadt is terribly wounded and entering torpor. What do you do?&quot;<br /> <br /> All Kindred around him: A shame if something happened to him.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but the &quot;and Pieterzoon&quot; part, it was overkill. I understand everyone hating Hardestadt but poor f..kboy Jan... really... XD (it really made me laugh hard)<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T00:26:48-07:00","id":1419528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1419524#post1419524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah but the &quot;and Pieterzoon&quot; part, it was overkill. I understand everyone hating Hardestadt but poor f..kboy Jan... really... XD (it really made me laugh hard)<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked that Theo Bell adamantly maintains he didn't kill Jan.<br /> <br /> So who did?<br /> <br /> Mind you, it's almost certain that Jan was the guy who helped Theo Bell kill Hardelstadt, IMHO. It just went pear shaped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T05:57:52-07:00","id":1419568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1419504#post1419504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What exactly do you think is the lost power?<br /> <br /> Frankly, STs should have some flexibility about what power you lose with a combo discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Must admit i'm still scratching my head trying to make sense of it. What he was trying to say that i'm completely missing the sense of. I'm going to point out one case in particular for example, but the doubt kind of goes for them all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1419501#post1419501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>And then eliminate your chance to buy the power that let you read auras. Forever.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, what part of &quot;the combo requires Auspex 4, ergo, the user <i><b>already </b></i>has the power to read auras&quot; was somehow missed?<br /> Or is there some nuance of player x ST interaction i'm missing here, care to explain?<br /> <br /> I'm honestly <b>not </b>understanding the rationale of why a character having any of the combos described - that basically are just <i>already existing</i> powers taken out of the &quot;elder powers&quot; straightjacket, damn, the whole point of the list was calling out the straightjacket - would result in elimination of the cited options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-22-2020, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T06:53:18-07:00","id":1419573,"title":"","content":"Well it depends. In V5 your only allowed 1 power per dot than before right? You could have Auspex 4 in V5, but instead of learning the alternate ability too that is listed in the same dot, your mysteriously locked out of learning both for... whatever reason. This is in stout contrast where each dot let you unlock a trove of powers in a bundle as you got more proficient in an ability. So this Amalgam system doesn't emulate the previous Elder abilities at all due to its laughable limitations and use on &quot;combos&quot; just to achieve &quot;Elder feats&quot;. Even more laughable when Ancillae or mid-Neonates (or MORE funnily enough Thin-bloods) with atleast 5 dots in two different disciplines can now supposedly achieve &quot;Elder&quot; level feats with this new mechanic logic...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 10-23-2020, 05:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T13:28:24-07:00","id":1419635,"title":"","content":"In my opinion, the only thing needed to bring back nasty Elder power is a rule allowing vampires of sufficient Generation and/or Blood Potency to purchase more than five powers per Discipline.<br /> <br /> Ancestral Dominion is a level 4/ Amalgam Blood Sorcery 3 power that is the same as the old level 9 Dominate the Descendants (or whatever the hell it was called). Can Neonates get it? Sure, but why? You haven't been around long enough to have enough descendants to make it worth while.<br /> <br /> Now that we have a solid example of a previous level 9 power it stands to reason until a future supplement comes out, we can make up our own.<br /> <br /> Even if we don't get rules for multiple powers, it has already been hinted at under Helena's description that perhaps resisting the Beckoning reduces your previous ability. I for one like the idea that as the Antediluvians wake, they draw their blood (power) back to themselves. You can go ride along with them, keep your power and be a puppet, or you can fight against it, but lose some of your previous blood god abilities. Either choice can make for interesting Elder/Methuselah level play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T14:39:24-07:00","id":1419647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1419568#post1419568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Must admit i'm still scratching my head trying to make sense of it. What he was trying to say that i'm completely missing the sense of. I'm going to point out one case in particular for example, but the doubt kind of goes for them all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Uh, what part of &quot;the combo requires Auspex 4, ergo, the user <i><b>already </b></i>has the power to read auras&quot; was somehow missed?<br /> Or is there some nuance of player x ST interaction i'm missing here, care to explain?<br /> <br /> I'm honestly <b>not </b>understanding the rationale of why a character having any of the combos described - that basically are just <i>already existing</i> powers taken out of the &quot;elder powers&quot; straightjacket, damn, the whole point of the list was calling out the straightjacket - would result in elimination of the cited options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Each vampire can only have five powers in each discipline. <br /> <br /> If you have purchased the power to read auras, your level four slot is occupied. If you want to buy an almagam, you can no longer use slot 4 for this, as it is already filled (by Aura View). You will have to use the level 5 slot to it. Then, you won't be able to buy any level 5 power because all your slots are already occupied.<br /> amalgam OCCUPY space in its known disciplines. So, a vampire would need to choose an power to sacrifice (never learn) to learn your amalgam.<br /> In v5, your maximum is 5 powers for each discipline. Understood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T15:14:52-07:00","id":1419656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1419647#post1419647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Each vampire can only have five powers in each discipline.<br /> <br /> If you have purchased the power to read auras, your level four slot is occupied. If you want to buy an almagam, you can no longer use slot 4 for this, as it is already filled (by Aura View). You will have to use the level 5 slot to it. Then, you won't be able to buy any level 5 power because all your slots are already occupied.<br /> amalgam OCCUPY space in its known disciplines. So, a vampire would need to choose an power to sacrifice (never learn) to learn your amalgam.<br /> In v5, your maximum is 5 powers for each discipline. Understood?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No ofense, but i'm reasonably sure you're mixing up with stuff like alternate forms for Gangrel and some similar things, because that's definitely NOT as discipline combos work. Like, <b>at all</b>. They do not replace <i>anything </i>and have costs in xp as powers their own.<br /> <br /> The kind of substitution you are proposing would make no sense whatsoever considering they base themselves in the <b><i>combination </i></b>of disciplines' knowledge so (with rare exceptions) require <b>two </b>of them, if not three, as in some uncommon but canon examples....<br /> <br /> They are kind of comparable to Sphere rotes from Mage the Ascension (take that with a grain of salt, i haven't played Mage since the turn of the millenium at least), though the potential to develop them is far from common knowledge among the kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-22-2020, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T00:32:05-07:00","id":1419730,"title":"","content":"No. he's right. In V5 If a power was Auspex 2, Dominate 4, I'd be using my 4th or 5th dot of dominate to buy it. <br /> <br /> In V1-20, combo disciplines don't take slots. You can stack as many as you want. Some disciplines do have rules for multiple powers each level too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T02:46:41-07:00","id":1419750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1419730#post1419730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. he's right. In V5 If a power was Auspex 2, Dominate 4, I'd be using my 4th or 5th dot of dominate to buy it.<br /> <br /> In V1-20, combo disciplines don't take slots. You can stack as many as you want. Some disciplines do have rules for multiple powers each level too.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the very reason why I don't understand people like the V5 discipline system. Its so restrictive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T04:38:20-07:00","id":1419760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1419750#post1419750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the very reason why I don't understand people like the V5 discipline system. Its so restrictive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Things I like about the V5 discipline system: <br /> Nothing is overpowered for it's level. <br /> It's got that 'one more level' kinda setup that keeps you addicted (or it would, were XP more common) <br /> <br /> Problems with the V5 discipline system (as constructively as I can put it):<br /> Overchoice; needing to put far too much consideration into which specific powers you want. So many possibilities is offputting; what if I take the 'wrong' power? . <br /> Overcomplicated<br /> Unreasonably specific powers, the whole thing feels less organic and more gamified. Disciplines are less an extension of the vampire's self and more a diverse set of perks and powers to unlock. They're far more like werewolf's gifts than a power you develop yourself. <br /> Disciplines have weaker themes. Celerity used to be just one thing, now it's anything speed or dexterity related. Animalism was control over Beast and beast, now it encompasses anything slightly to do with either. Quietus is just weird magic now. <br /> Physical disciplines are just as complicated as thaumaturgy now. The people who play brujah for simplicity are in for a hard time, and the people who play Tremere to be a wizard? Forget it. <br /> Weak power level wise; You'd be better off increasing your dice pools in a lot of cases. Methuselah are not accomadated for. <br /> single dots with diverse offerings (auspex 1) are now spread among many dots. Meaning I will have far fewer abilities at level 5 in this edition. <br /> No Thaumaturgy/necromancy. (yeah, nah; Sorcery and Oblivion are not good replacements) <br /> Mergers causing a loss of clan identity and deny a lot of power potential (Before I could have 5 thaumaturgy and 5 quietus, now I only have 5 sorcery!) <br /> Mergers screw with the story (assamite caste system? Lasombra and Giovanni once being long-lost twins? Obtenebration's abyss is from the underworld and it was<i> this</i> obvious all this time?) <br /> The lack of 6+ disciplines curbs ambition and reduces the chance of diablerie. <br /> Being able to have your own special powers from 1-5 also curbs my desire to get a level 6 discipline. <br /> Using a blood or not for a power used to have thematic metaphysical reasons. Now it's just a matter of balance.<br /> It's a lot harder to remember who's got what at your table. <br /> Combo disciplines are even more of a pain to get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T05:10:15-07:00","id":1419766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lack of 6+ disciplines curbs ambition and reduces the chance of diablerie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ding, ding, ding! Part of the whole risk factor benefit of diablerie was getting more supernaturally strong than you possibly could've if you were a higher generation. Even more for getting some higher points in a discipline you never even knew of before, adding onto the base your clan starts with or anything you learned from an outside teacher. It perfectly simulated the need for the young to try and topple the old and subsume their power, even with the risks. Now from a meta-gameplay point, no one would want to diablerize because now its all risks with no benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T15:31:38-07:00","id":1419856,"title":"","content":"Diablerie is still a legit route to power, it's just way more risky because of the new rules for being taken over. The only drawback to higher Blood Potency is the feeding restrictions, and that's not a problem if you don't care about killing a human (or vampire) to drop your Hunger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T01:57:52-07:00","id":1419943,"title":"","content":"Diablerie is a moron's game in V5.<br /> <br /> paradoxically, disablerie rewards high humanity vampires devouring high generation vampires for discipline dots. Devouring vampires for generation will fuck you up. Devouring vampires with low humanity gives you increased risks and decreased rewards so you're going to stop doing it once you get to 5 humanity and never do it again.<br /> <br /> Blood potency is a bad thing. It increases hunger and decreases the food available to you, all for a few measly dice.<br /> <br /> So the thing is, it's not even a legit path to power. If you farm the right resonances you can get multiple 5th level disciplines before you hit anciillae so diablerie really is just a quick and dirty to something you don't even have to wait that long for.<br /> <br /> <br /> (I calculated this somewhere else, not going to bother to do it here, but I worked under the assumption that: you need to wait for the resonance to recover with the Red blood cells, and that you get the same resonance each time. on later reading, It's more likely that resonances cycle but you can feed one point each night, which is far, far, far better. Worst and least likely case is random resonances every six weeks, but you can make up for that with quantity. The point being discipline xp is cheap so you don't need to diablerize for it )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T04:38:32-07:00","id":1419958,"title":"","content":"Haven't read up on Resonance farming, but it sounds interesting. If Diablerie incurred Stains, not automatic loss, it'd be worth it. I don't see the feeding restriction as an issue because if you're already a serial Diablerist, killing humans (or vampires) to drop Hunger won't be an issue.<br /> <br /> I am curious if there is some errata for it. I just noticed that the Bahari Loresheet mentions the roll is Humanity+Resolve+Blood Potency, while in Diablerie description it says Humanity+Resolve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T05:31:50-07:00","id":1419968,"title":"","content":"Using humanity in the roll to gain powers from diablerie is crazy for a multitude of reasons. If anything, being closer to the beast should gain you more than being further away. <br /> <br /> I think possession is silly and gaining discipline xp through diablerie is the best way to destroy the dynamic of a party. But If I had to do a roll for possession, it'd be like this. <br /> <br /> Victim rolls Willpower+Generation MINUS the diablerist's willpower+Generation Versus the Diablerist's willpower+Generation in a contested roll. <br /> <br /> So, Tom has a willpower of 4 and is 12th generation (so has 1 dot) and is eaten by Jerry (who has 8 willpower and is 13th gen, so 0. Tom's 5 is reduced by 8 to 0; he has absolutely no chance of possessing jerry. If we switched these values around, Tom (8+0) eats jerry ( 4+1). Jerry has 3 dice (8-5) to 'possess' jerry (8). <br /> Successes <br /> 1- Diablerist gets a few vibrant memories and to a degree gains few desires that were strong in the victim (protect/hurt someone in particular). They may dream the victim's life. <br /> 2-More memories, some useful habits and mannerisms come through. <br /> 3- Nature changes to that of the victim. The memories mash together. the diablerist retains control<br /> 4- The victim has edged out dominance. The Diablerist's consciousness exists in the back of their mind. <br /> 5- perfect possession. <br /> <br /> Basically, you don't get possessed unless your will is very weak or you bite off <i>way</i> more than you can chew. You are chewing: A diablerist should have a big advantage over their victim. Possession should be rare and rumoured. (but also siring childer just to diablerize you, as golconda seekers often do, should be possible)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T09:19:11-07:00","id":1420132,"title":"","content":"I agree that Humanity shouldn't be in the roll, I just see that there is currently a discrepancy with RAW and that one (if the actual rule adds Humanity) at least gives the Diablerist an advantage.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'd rather revise the V20 rules in the Tal Mahe Ra book and use them for V5. Because just at a cursory glance, you're better off farming XP from Dyscrasia. Currently, RAW, assuming you plan carefully and take down one vampire/year, you still get more XP farming blood (yea, this is all metagaming, but still...).<br /> <br /> Now that I've derailed the original topic, I still stand firm that we have enough examples in the current books for V5 to make the old Elder level powers. What we need is a way for Elders to develop more than 5 powers per Discipline. Or maybe not. With the current rules, you have something like this Elder has Dominate and Presence 5, needs only his voice and can send commands down the line.<br /> <br /> But this Neonate, can develop new powers to hunt in this age because he hasn't maxed out Disciplines. So his Presence reaches over media, and his Obfuscate fools electronics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T11:21:09-07:00","id":1420148,"title":"","content":"<i>Funny mental image: The elders were playing the game wrong and the beckoning is a game master giving them time-out.<br /> <br /> Caine sits behind a GM screen and his ancient players are told to either reduce their stats or get sent to Syria. </i><br /> <br /> On topic:<br /> The TBH 20th book's alt rules for diablerie are also bad.<br /> <br /> As for farming Dyscrasia.... I feel like I'd get annoyed if the players at the table did that? Especially if one player knows how to game the system/shop smart and the others aren't on the same page and either aren't near-as good or have moral objections or... and then they'll fight over who's hoarding the XP closet and...<br /> Nah I kinda love it when my players infight a little. The real issue is that resonance farming isn't all that quantified and a storyteller might make resonances common and convenient or rare, unpredictable, difficult to harvest, and sure to lead to conflict.<br /> <br /> I don't really like the obtuse medieval categorization or the idea that happiness gives you presence.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of learning disciplines through feeding. But for me it's far more interesting and thematically appropriate to the identity of every clan and bloodline to have <i>the way you feed</i> give you disciplines. Use your authority to get blood? Dominate. Sneakily feed from a sleeping victim? Obfuscate. Rare disciplines are a matter of exotic blood or practice.<br /> You go after specific people to increase your attributes and certain talents. A vampire would heal any workout they do, and how else could you become more intelligent? Vampires are parasites and they take from those who have. Clan Toreador sabotage the careers of thousands of talented artists and performers each night; denying them exposure so that the vampires can keep a good drink for themselves.<br /> <br /> If we wanted to give XP through this. we could say every 10 points of blood grants 1 xp in the appropriate discipline, maybe diminish the returns for excessive feeding (So you don't get your first dot by draining ten people in a single night... but maybe 20 or 30 would be permissible. Not sure. They're almost certainly going to attract attention for that kind of thing, maybe we could let them have it? It's one way of encouraging the Beast) You could similarly have vampires earn xp for attributes and feeding from the right people..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 10-25-2020, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T00:15:15-07:00","id":1420220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1419760#post1419760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unreasonably specific powers, the whole thing feels less organic and more gamified. Disciplines are less an extension of the vampire's self and more a diverse set of perks and powers to unlock. They're far more like werewolf's gifts than a power you develop yourself.<br /> <br /> Combo disciplines are even more of a pain to get.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think this has something to do with the devs being more into developing video games for OWOD now, rather than tabletop experiences?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake","name":"NuclearSnake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25604_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T01:06:01-07:00","id":1420222,"title":"","content":"Yes and No.<br /> <br /> Yes, because current game design emphasizes a constant stream of rewards and so lots of very noticable little things get your brain juiced up on dopamine. You could for example compare Skyrim to the two TES games before it: Lot's of big messages every time you level up, a perk every level and so on. It's just how the big wigs want it so you get an addictive possitive feedback loop. And V5 has clearly been taking notes.<br /> <br /> <br /> No, Because that shit's hard as fuck to code. OG potence/Celerity/Fortitude just work miles better in that they're easier to code in, design UI for, and easier on the control scheme.<br /> <br /> edit: besides that, gameplay decisions in a computer game mean less for the story than choices made for a tabletop rpg. In Halo for example the Assault rifle does less damage per shot than the pistol fpr gameplay reasons even though that isn't realistic. the lore/story is still taken seriously, we are more willing to accept Pistols&gt;Assault rifles thanks to the medium, in which creating a fun and therefor balanced sandbox of weapons and abilities is priority. In a storytelling tabletop game, such a sandbox a lesser concern, and the players are more likely to get frustrated when a choice breaks immersion or an npc can do something against the rules that they cannot. so it's a pretty bad idea all round to change a tabletop's rules for your video game.<br /> The Miracle of Vampire's first edition is that it managed to have kick ass mechanics that added to and built upon the fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 10-26-2020, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T01:57:25-07:00","id":1420227,"title":"","content":"hehehe... Caine and his players, that's funny. Until/if we get Elder level rules, I really think a simple fix is allowing an extra power based on Blood Potency. You can tweak it however you want; every even dot, every dot, only extra powers in your Clan Disciplines...<br /> <br /> I also like that idea you had about XP for Attributes too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T13:46:15-07:00","id":1420323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PJ123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1420227#post1420227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hehehe... Caine and his players, that's funny. Until/if we get Elder level rules, I really think a simple fix is allowing an extra power based on Blood Potency. You can tweak it however you want; every even dot, every dot, only extra powers in your Clan Disciplines...<br /> <br /> I also like that idea you had about XP for Attributes too.</div> </div> </div> </div>My preferred way is just to run the V20 system with the V5 metaplot changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake","name":"NuclearSnake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25604_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T13:54:31-07:00","id":1420324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1420222#post1420222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes and No.<br /> <br /> Yes, because current game design emphasizes a constant stream of rewards and so lots of very noticable little things get your brain juiced up on dopamine. You could for example compare Skyrim to the two TES games before it: Lot's of big messages every time you level up, a perk every level and so on. It's just how the big wigs want it so you get an addictive possitive feedback loop. And V5 has clearly been taking notes.<br /> <br /> <br /> No, Because that shit's hard as fuck to code. OG potence/Celerity/Fortitude just work miles better in that they're easier to code in, design UI for, and easier on the control scheme.<br /> <br /> edit: besides that, gameplay decisions in a computer game mean less for the story than choices made for a tabletop rpg. In Halo for example the Assault rifle does less damage per shot than the pistol fpr gameplay reasons even though that isn't realistic. the lore/story is still taken seriously, we are more willing to accept Pistols&gt;Assault rifles thanks to the medium, in which creating a fun and therefor balanced sandbox of weapons and abilities is priority. In a storytelling tabletop game, such a sandbox a lesser concern, and the players are more likely to get frustrated when a choice breaks immersion or an npc can do something against the rules that they cannot. so it's a pretty bad idea all round to change a tabletop's rules for your video game.<br /> The Miracle of Vampire's first edition is that it managed to have kick ass mechanics that added to and built upon the fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMHO, many of the changes made to the game, the removal of elder level powers, the removal of a lot of disciplines and bloodlines, and the eradication of the Sabbat/marginalization of the Camarilla seem like attempts to simplify the game to me. Maybe to market it to a broader audience? The old mechanics were pretty much ok the way they were, nobody had any complaints about it as they do for V5 mechanics, and you know what they say, if it ain't broke don't fix it. Maybe it's just middle managment syndrome, people making changes just because they can? Not trying to slag on the devs here, I'm just genuinely perplexed as to why they would make so many controversial changes, so unnecessarily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake","name":"NuclearSnake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25604_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T14:17:27-07:00","id":1420328,"title":"","content":"V5 hasn't streamlined anything though. If anything it's the opposite Character creation is a lot more work. Disciplines are technically fewer in number but in practice they are a lot more complicated because you have so many options: Disciplines used to be 1,2,3,4,5; now I gotta go through them like &quot;1c,1b,3a,4a,4b. Not to mention a few disciplines were really simple and essentially one power, or I only used one or two powers. <br /> <br /> As for accessibility... Sects are now 'easy'. The elders have buggered off and a lot of stuff has been pushed to blacks and whites rather than shades of gray. There's less presure to conform, less 'tough spot' stuff, less careful manuevering. it's &quot;We're the freedom team and those guys are our ideological opposite; don't think too hard about this&quot; <br /> But dealing with a lot of stuff is harder. Beastial crits, the game's difficulty for dice rolls being about 1 or 2 too high all the time, a lot of disciplines are weaker so mortals are far more threatening and night-to-night living becomes a scarier prospect than the elders and sleeping methuselahs that once (D)dominated your existence. I'd say it's less accessible, really. Especially if you're not on the same page ideologically and you can't stand either type of Settite or whatever when you once embraced the glories of Set like no tomorrow. (They really got Osiris'd) <br /> <br /> It's a harder game, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T18:38:55-07:00","id":1420374,"title":"","content":"They didn't remove Elder level Disciplines, we just now have a max of 5 powers per Discipline. Some of them are the old Elder powers, retooled.<br /> <br /> I don't like Character Creation. I wish they'd gone like CoD with flat costs, because it seems like to avoid min-maxing they just told you 'this is where your points go'. I like the choices among Disciplines, because now in-game and meta game, you don't always know what your opponent may have.<br /> <br /> The power level across the board has been toned down, and that's okay too. Elders and Methuselahs are scary, but no longer indestructible blood gods. And that makes things like the Anarch Revolt and other kindred wars more believable. The young really can take out the old.<br /> <br /> And I get that some people don't like these changes. That's okay too. There are things about V5 I don't like, but I've seen enough of you get kicked off topics for that so I'm keeping my mouth shut. \ud83d\ude01","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T18:44:36-07:00","id":1420377,"title":"","content":"Elders and Methuselahs in this edition aren't scary whatsoever. Some of them are literally non-existent with the Beckoning as of now. We also literally went over this- Elder Disciplines are practically gone at this point and I don't know why you claim otherwise. In this thread alone we already went over that. The power level tone-down definitely wasn't okay because now as this very OP thread post brings up, previous feats found in the previous editions simply aren't possible anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T18:56:01-07:00","id":1420382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PJ123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1420374#post1420374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They didn't remove Elder level Disciplines, we just now have a max of 5 powers per Discipline. Some of them are the old Elder powers, retooled.<br /> <br /> The power level across the board has been toned down, and that's okay too. Elders and Methuselahs are scary, but no longer indestructible blood gods. And that makes things like the Anarch Revolt and other kindred wars more believable. The young really can take out the old.</div> </div> </div> </div>The young were supposed to take out the old and through sheer weight of numbers, not mano y mano. What reason is there to rebel against one's elders if everyone can reach the approximate same power level eventually? If anything it makes the Anarch revolt make less sense, not more. Now it just seems like a bunch of brats massacring their sires for no other reason than a lack of patience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake","user":"NuclearSnake","date":". 10-26-2020, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake","name":"NuclearSnake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25604_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T20:36:36-07:00","id":1420396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuclearSnake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1420382#post1420382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The young were supposed to take out the old and through sheer weight of numbers, not mano y mano. What reason is there to rebel against one's elders if everyone can reach the approximate same power level eventually? If anything it makes the Anarch revolt make less sense, not more. Now it just seems like a bunch of brats massacring their sires for no other reason than a lack of patience.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because you still can't. Your Generation still imposes a concrete ceiling on you. Even if you and a Methuselah have the same Discipline spread, that Methuselah is going to stomp you because of their Generation. They're adding 3-5 dice to most Discipline rolls, where youngers are adding 1 or 2; they're healing multiple levels of Superficial damage while youngers are healing 1 or 2; they are adding 3-5 dice to any Attribute roll when they blood surge/buff. Elders and Methuselahs are scary in the mechanics built, even without RPG Boss Moves like 'I spit acid!' or 'I summon things that make a localized earthquake!' The math makes them terrifying, even against multiple opponents. Especially if you play them smart as they should be, not 'press A to Attack' RPG Boss Monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T21:42:46-07:00","id":1420403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuclearSnake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1420382#post1420382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The young were supposed to take out the old and through sheer weight of numbers, not mano y mano. What reason is there to rebel against one's elders if everyone can reach the approximate same power level eventually? If anything it makes the Anarch revolt make less sense, not more. Now it just seems like a bunch of brats massacring their sires for no other reason than a lack of patience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, being treated like crap for 200 years and fed to the Inquisition seems a good reason to rebel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T05:18:03-07:00","id":1420431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Your Generation still imposes a concrete ceiling on you. Even if you and a Methuselah have the same Discipline spread, that Methuselah is going to stomp you because of their Generation.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Dude, that's what diablerie is for lol. You don't fight the scary ass uber Methuselahs off the bat, you work your way down by taking out Elders of reasonable power, but still not too much to just clobber you or your entire coterie at once in seconds. Then when the Generation gap continues to close then you'd be able to go up against Methuselahs with the same Discipline spread.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T05:57:43-07:00","id":1420438,"title":"","content":"Elmerg made a good point of clarifying what I meant about the young taking out the old. Only thing I'm adding is I never said Mano y Mano, I said the mechanics now support the possibility of it happening. Oh, and thanks to Blood Potency, the young are going to hit Hunger 5 before said Elder (because Discipline Rouse check re-rolls).<br /> <br /> Shakanaka, what do you define as Elder level power? Because V5 took a previously 9th level Dominate and made it a 4th level Amalgam. It still does the same thing, just theoretically a 13th Generation vampire could develop it (but why, it'd be a waste; not enough descendants).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T06:16:07-07:00","id":1420444,"title":"","content":"That's exactly why this system is borked. 13th gen should NEVER be able to do a 9 level Dominate, that's the most ludicrous thing ever. Amalgams aren't a replacement for Elder Disciplines whatsover- they were never combinations of two or more disciplines, but sovereign on their own. This does nothing to adequately simulate the past edition, just a lame ghetto version. The mechanics of the previous edition DID support ways for the young taking out the old, but it was realistic. To even take out an Elder or even a METHUSELAH for that matter take decades of planning in advance, it wasn't just something that HAPPENED unless it was a Siege (are these even a thing now with the Sabbat gone?). This is now just pure clownery.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25604_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25604\" data-vbnamecard=\"25604\">NuclearSnake</a> made this point aswell, if we went by V5 logic there wouldn't be no Anarch revolt or revolts at all if their childe can get strong like this with no logic at all, because everyone basically has the same tier of power basically. The reason for the mass revolts and researching ways to break the blood-bound was that so the young could band together to even fight against the Elders- and it worked to a degree. Now in a V5 paradigm it doesn't make sense for the young to have teamed up because they could've clobbed their sires eventually. The 5 cap is literally just Neonate-Ancillae tier, they shouldn't be able to use Elder disciplines with this &quot;Amalgam&quot; nonsense at all it they coincidently had two 5 Disciplines in their suite. 6+ represented the might of the Elders and Methuselahs along with their natural proficiencies to hold domain in the first place, but now none of that is here (with the Beckoning and all).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T06:50:08-07:00","id":1420455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1420444#post1420444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's exactly why this system is borked. 13th gen should NEVER be able to do a 9 level Dominate, that's the most ludicrous thing ever. Amalgams aren't a replacement for Elder Disciplines whatsover- they were never combinations of two or more disciplines, but sovereign on their own. This does nothing to adequately simulate the past edition, just a lame ghetto version. The mechanics of the previous edition DID support ways for the young taking out the old, but it was realistic. To even take out an Elder or even a METHUSELAH for that matter take decades of planning in advance, it wasn't just something that HAPPENED unless it was a Siege (are these even a thing now with the Sabbat gone?). This is now just pure clownery.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25604_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25604\" data-vbnamecard=\"25604\">NuclearSnake</a> made this point aswell, if we went by V5 logic there wouldn't be no Anarch revolt or revolts at all if their childe can get strong like this with no logic at all, because everyone basically has the same tier of power basically. The reason for the mass revolts and researching ways to break the blood-bound was that so the young could band together to even fight against the Elders- and it worked to a degree. Now in a V5 paradigm it doesn't make sense for the young to have teamed up because they could've clobbed their sires eventually. The 5 cap is literally just Neonate-Ancillae tier, they shouldn't be able to use Elder disciplines with this &quot;Amalgam&quot; nonsense at all it they coincidently had two 5 Disciplines in their suite. 6+ represented the might of the Elders and Methuselahs along with their natural proficiencies to hold domain in the first place, but now none of that is here (with the Beckoning and all).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is ignoring the point of Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> Also, what 13th generation vampire is going to have multiple 5 level disciplines?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T08:20:18-07:00","id":1420482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PJ123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1420438#post1420438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elmerg made a good point of clarifying what I meant about the young taking out the old. Only thing I'm adding is I never said Mano y Mano, I said the mechanics now support the possibility of it happening. Oh, and thanks to Blood Potency, the young are going to hit Hunger 5 before said Elder (because Discipline Rouse check re-rolls).<br /> <br /> Shakanaka, what do you define as Elder level power? Because V5 took a previously 9th level Dominate and made it a 4th level Amalgam. It still does the same thing, just theoretically a 13th Generation vampire could develop it (but why, it'd be a waste; not enough descendants).</div> </div> </div> </div>Do not replicate on a 1:1 scale.<br /> <br /> V5 version is way weaker. Just saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T09:52:46-07:00","id":1420494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1420455#post1420455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this is ignoring the point of Blood Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood<br /> Potency<br /> Is<br /> Shit. <br /> <br /> The extra dice are not worth the now quantified drawbacks of potency; namely more hunger and a diminished source of food. The sweet spot of 'this is good' is between BP 1 and 4. Diminishing returns is severe. Sure, you might get... a whoping 3 extra dice when you go beyond this level, but is it worth the extra hunger? The lack of blood? <br /> <br /> I am looking at the fucking table, and yeah, getting past 5th level potency is like having a gigantic penis the size of a child (at 10th level you probably have an adult sized wang) sure it may be impressive and even intimidating, but you aren't going to have much, if any, sex with it. It just causes problems. <br /> <br /> I'm sorry for the vulgar analogy, but I just don't fucking see how you can look at the same table I'm looking at and don't realise what an absolute fucking downer high blood pontency is in this game. It is not worth it. There is more curse than blessing. More healing and a few more dice are not worth the massive drawbacks. Imagine having an option to make more money but to do so you have to be fucking starving all the time, everything tastes worse to you, and in general you've got to lower your standard of living and shut yourself away more often? You are winning a dick measuring contest with potency in V5; but nobody wants sex to be worse than childbirth. <br /> <br /> I... just can't articulate the full extent of how fucking undesirable blood potency is. It's terrible. It's just fucking terrible. Maybe people persecute thin bloods because they're jealous of a potential to actually be a happy vampire? Methuselah and Antideluvians are no doubt in Torpor all the time because they're miserable with this shit and wish themselves below their minimum.. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, what 13th generation vampire is going to have multiple 5 level disciplines? </div> </div> </div>Pretty easy answer there; one that's stayed around long enough and hasn't diablerized? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T10:31:12-07:00","id":1420508,"title":"","content":"Blood Potency was only brought in because when they rebooted VTM they just clobbered stuff from VTR without thinking of how to properly make it work. The new devs can like stuff from VTR, but I don't think they accounted that the audiences for both lines are decidedly different and the mechanics for the gamelines itself are different as well. There was no reason to add Blood Potency to VTM, it makes no sense.<br /> <br /> I assume they only incorporated it as some way to solve the Generation meta (haven't I mentioned this before? Hm, I forgot) because obviously the common denominator as time go on will be high gens and by fault they aren't viable whatsoever. So they flipped the whole setting and made everything has a fault-line weaker to where its just pretty.. mushy now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T11:00:30-07:00","id":1420521,"title":"","content":"I feel it's either a call for equality; A 13th gen is just as good as a 3rd and it's a matter of tradeoffs, or you're supposed to think vampires are bad, being more vampire is worse, and the only good ending is one where you become human again; diablerie is an affront to God and a trap option of the adversary; each generation removed from caine is a mercy and offers more chance to find redemption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T15:12:42-07:00","id":1420558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1419730#post1419730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. he's right. In V5 If a power was Auspex 2, Dominate 4, I'd be using my 4th or 5th dot of dominate to buy it.<br /> <br /> In V1-20, combo disciplines don't take slots. You can stack as many as you want. Some disciplines do have rules for multiple powers each level too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, that explains much (boneheaded as it may sound). Another reason to keep V5 at arm's length and stick to doing my mostly old fart own thing, it seems....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T02:29:38-08:00","id":1421573,"title":"","content":"If it's not too late to suggest something relating to the original question, the closest I can come up with for a broader explanation for the absence of Methuselah powers is to broaden the V5 experience of Helena, who felt 'lesser' by resisting the Beckoning. If that was meant to be a wider result (or future game mechanic) for Elders and Meth's resisting the Beckoning, then the in-game justification could be in order for a powerful vampire to resist the Beckoning, their ability set gets knocked down to what conforms with V5 rules. Thus the Methuselah's had their fantastic, high level powers, preserving game lore, but due to the Beckoning, they are either out of the picture or reduced to V5 rule-set abilities. Not saying that I think this is a good explanation, but one that would work with what I've seen published so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25885-ozymandias242","name":"Ozymandias242","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T12:30:20-08:00","id":1422100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ozymandias242</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1421573#post1421573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's not too late to suggest something relating to the original question, the closest I can come up with for a broader explanation for the absence of Methuselah powers is to broaden the V5 experience of Helena, who felt 'lesser' by resisting the Beckoning. If that was meant to be a wider result (or future game mechanic) for Elders and Meth's resisting the Beckoning, then the in-game justification could be in order for a powerful vampire to resist the Beckoning, their ability set gets knocked down to what conforms with V5 rules. Thus the Methuselah's had their fantastic, high level powers, preserving game lore, but due to the Beckoning, they are either out of the picture or reduced to V5 rule-set abilities. Not saying that I think this is a good explanation, but one that would work with what I've seen published so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never quite understood why they couldn't have used the passage of the Red Star as the &quot;equalizer&quot;, reducing the eldest Kindred to V5 power levels without removing them from the setting altogether. It would have given player characters more of a chance to make their mark with less year-zero-isation of the setting. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T02:35:34-08:00","id":1422202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1420494#post1420494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am looking at the fucking table, and yeah, getting past 5th level potency is like having a gigantic penis the size of a child (at 10th level you probably have an adult sized wang) sure it may be impressive and even intimidating, but you aren't going to have much, if any, sex with it. It just causes problems.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry for the vulgar analogy, but I just don't fucking see how you can look at the same table I'm looking at and don't realise what an absolute fucking downer high blood pontency is in this game. It is not worth it. There is more curse than blessing. More healing and a few more dice are not worth the massive drawbacks. Imagine having an option to make more money but to do so you have to be fucking starving all the time, everything tastes worse to you, and in general you've got to lower your standard of living and shut yourself away more often? You are winning a dick measuring contest with potency in V5; but nobody wants sex to be worse than childbirth.<br /> <br /> I... just can't articulate the full extent of how fucking undesirable blood potency is. It's terrible. It's just fucking terrible. Maybe people persecute thin bloods because they're jealous of a potential to actually be a happy vampire? Methuselah and Antideluvians are no doubt in Torpor all the time because they're miserable with this shit and wish themselves below their minimum..</div> </div> </div> </div>Not arguing with you here, because essentially you're right. And if one would require the the game rules to accurately simulate the workings of the game world, then the system would be even more problematic, because many story events couldn't have happened the way they did, if there were RAW dice rolls involved.<br /> But up to a certain point this is a question of personal preference. I really value Ars Magica's system for its logical rules that can also simulate every single thing that ever happened, every spell cast, every ritual conducted and every mage tower built. If 5 different players at different places of the world think of the same magical effect and create a spell out of it, chances are that those 5 players will probably come up with the same spell rules wise after doing some calculations. This is awesome and something that i really value and that makes magic feel 'real' and 'scientific' in Ars Magica. But even V20 never had that. Granted it had more of that than V5, but it's miles away from Ars Magica. And that's ok, because VtM always had a stronger focus on character stuff and horror and metaplot etc.<br /> So for me VtM was always a system where I as a ST had to wing some things in sofar as it contributed to the story and overall gaming experience of the group. Coming from that position there are some things I can accept with V5's rules and can appreciate other changes, which shifted the focus on stuff that is narrative fun.<br /> <br /> Blood Potency is one of these things: When my players started having higher BP the experience shifted dramatically. The subjective difference in competence between BP 1 and BP 4 was larger than expected and the drawbacks concerning the feeding restrictions shifted the attention of the stories we played more often than not. It resulted in a lot of emergent stories. (Stories that weren't planned but resulted from messy criticals, bestial failures or a greater need to plan out hunting more explicitly.) Our experience with V5 hitherto was that it feels more like playing a vampire than most earlier editions. And that's something my players like. And it's something that's supported by the BP system.<br /> <br /> All those things obviously change nothing about the fact, that the points you criticised are Right. At least concerning the intention/angle of your criticism.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">&quot;Life's barely long enough to get good at one thing. So be careful what you get good at.&quot;</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26196-saturno","name":"Saturno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T03:06:37-08:00","id":1422206,"title":"","content":"It'd be interesting to hear from you after you've dangled some even lower generation vampires before them; see what happens at potency 5+ , if they even want take the opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T03:30:12-08:00","id":1422213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5?p=1422206#post1422206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It'd be interesting to hear from you after you've dangled some even lower generation vampires before them; see what happens at potency 5+ , if they even want take the opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Our next chronicle will probably be a camarilla chronicle with the characters being somewhere between 50 and 150 years. (Our chronicle at the moment is an anarch/Independent chronicle in Berlin with neonates.) Right now my only experience that I have with BP 5-7 is via the chronicle's antagonists. Maxwell Ldescu for example. But that's of course different than having player characters. I expect the 'elder game' to be quite different from prior editions. With more focus on feeding interaction (because of the BP rules and because of resonance/dyscrasias). That might not be everyones thing.<br /> <br /> Long story short: It could well be that we will introduce house rules to play a different kind of story when we arrive at BP 5+. But until now it serves our stories right.<br /> <br /> Edit: But the XP cost for raising BP should be way lower, because it's a double edged sword. That's something deserving of a change for the next printing of V5. Or something to house rule. As it is now, noone in their right might would pay BPx10 XP for that. Probably BPx4 or BPx5 at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">&quot;Life's barely long enough to get good at one thing. So be careful what you get good at.&quot;</span></div>","edited":{"userid":26196,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26196-saturno","user":"Saturno","date":". 11-06-2020, 06:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26196-saturno","name":"Saturno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T12:51:46-08:00","id":1422644,"title":"","content":"If we're talking Methuselah whats wrong with 'beyond 5th dot plot device?' It worked just as well for Vampire at 10 dot (nevermind other systems that had to face similar 'higher being' issues) and you can always borrow inspiration from other material (like the old 'higher than 5 dot' powers.) <br /> <br /> Other game systems (like Demon for the Earthbound) had options for boosting the power of high level beings even if some of their powers didn't go above 5 dots. In some cases those can be applicable too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}